    "type": "text",
    "text": "A good README answers questions in the order people ask them:\n\n1. **What is it** — one sentence and a screenshot.\n2. **Why** — what pain it removes and how it differs from alternatives.\n3. **How to run it** — three commands that definitely work.\n4. **How it works** — a diagram and links to the docs.\n5. **How to help** — CONTRIBUTING and good first issue labels.\n\nPoint 3 matters most: if the demo starts with one command, no keys and no setup, far more people will make it to point 4.",
